OVERVIEW: Update MPPS instance (N-SET)

USAGE: dicom-mpps update [<options>] <host> --aet <aet> --mpps-uid <mpps-uid> --status <status>

ARGUMENTS:
  <host>                  PACS server hostname or IP address, optionally with
                          port (host:port)

OPTIONS:
  --port <port>           PACS server port (default: 11112)
  --aet <aet>             Local Application Entity Title (calling AE)
  --called-aet <called-aet>
                          Remote Application Entity Title (default: ANY-SCP)
                          (default: ANY-SCP)
  --mpps-uid <mpps-uid>   MPPS SOP Instance UID to update
  --status <status>       New Performed Procedure Step Status (0040,0252):
                          COMPLETED or DISCONTINUED (PS3.3 Table C.4-14; PS3.4
                          F.7.2.2.2 — final, no later N-SET). COMPLETED
                          requires at least one Performed Series item
                          (--series-uid with --image-uid), PS3.4 Table F.7.2-1
                          final state
  --study-uid <study-uid> Study Instance UID for referenced images
  --series-uid <series-uid>
                          Series Instance UID for referenced images
  --image-uid <image-uid> SOP Instance UID (0008,1155) of a referenced image,
                          repeatable; needs --study-uid and --series-uid to
                          form the Performed Series item
  --sop-class-uid <sop-class-uid>
                          Actual SOP Class UID (0008,1150) of every referenced
                          image, e.g. 1.2.840.10008.5.1.4.1.1.2 for CT.
                          Required with --image-uid; no class is inferred
  --protocol-name <protocol-name>
                          Protocol Name (0018,1030) — Type 1 in every Performed
                          Series item (default: UNSPECIFIED)
  --series-description <series-description>
                          Series Description (0008,103E) for the performed
                          series
  --operator-name <operator-name>
                          Operators' Name (0008,1070), DICOM PN format
  --performing-physician <performing-physician>
                          Performing Physician's Name (0008,1050), DICOM PN
                          format
  --legacy-nset-scheduled-attributes
                          Also send the Scheduled Step Attributes Sequence
                          (0040,0270) in the N-SET. PS3.4 forbids it; use only
                          for an SCP known to require it
  --discontinuation-reason <discontinuation-reason>
                          Performed Procedure Step Discontinuation Reason Code
                          Sequence (0040,0281) as CODE|SCHEME|MEANING, only
                          with --status DISCONTINUED. Codes normally come from
                          PS3.16 CID 9300 'Procedure Discontinuation Reason'
                          (which includes CID 9301) with scheme DCM, e.g.
                          "110513|DCM|Discontinued for unspecified reason",
                          "110500|DCM|Doctor canceled procedure",
                          "110501|DCM|Equipment failure", "110507|DCM|Patient
                          did not arrive"
  --specific-character-set <specific-character-set>
                          Force the Specific Character Set (0008,0005), e.g.
                          ISO_IR 100 or ISO_IR 192. By default the narrowest
                          set that represents every text value is chosen
  --timeout <timeout>     Connection timeout in seconds (default: 60) (default:
                          60)
  -v, --verbose           Show verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

